# Chrome Bookmark AI Structuring & Transactional Tree Architecture

Condensed engineering patterns distilled from SOTA Chrome extensions (`bcollard/chrome-advanced-bookmarks`, `migsilva89/MarkMind`, `PanHywel/TidyMark`, `Fannon/search-bookmarks-history-and-tabs`, `isandrel/bookmark-scout`).

---

## 1. Fast Fuzzy Subsequence Search & Folder Guessing
*Source: `bcollard/chrome-advanced-bookmarks`*

### Fuzzy Subsequence Scoring
```typescript
export function fuzzyScore(pattern: string, text: string): number {
  const p = pattern.toLowerCase();
  const t = text.toLowerCase();
  let score = 0, pIdx = 0, prevMatchIdx = -2;

  for (let i = 0; i < t.length && pIdx < p.length; i++) {
    if (t[i] === p[pIdx]) {
      score += 10;
      if (prevMatchIdx === i - 1) score += 15; // Consecutive match bonus
      if (i === 0 || t[i - 1] === ' ' || t[i - 1] === '/' || t[i - 1] === '-') score += 20; // Word start bonus
      prevMatchIdx = i;
      pIdx++;
    } else {
      score -= 1; // Gap penalty
    }
  }
  return pIdx === p.length ? Math.max(1, score) : 0;
}
```

### Folder Auto-Detection (`findBestFolderForTitle`)
- Split bookmark title into meaningful tokens (stopword filtered, length > 2).
- Score each folder path against title tokens.
- Select highest scoring folder (above threshold) as default target when `Alt+D` is triggered.

