## 2. Safe LLM Batching & Two-Tier Triage
*Sources: `migsilva89/MarkMind`, `PanHywel/TidyMark`*

### Two-Tier Triage
1. **Tier 1 (Instant Offline Rules)**: Fast deterministic matching by domain/regex (e.g. `github.com` -> `Dev/Repositories`, `figma.com` -> `Design/Workspaces`).
2. **Tier 2 (Batched LLM Reorganization)**: Unmatched bookmarks are chunked into batches of 25–40 items to stay safely within prompt token limits.

### Schema Constrained Prompt Contract
```typescript
export interface OrganizeSuggestion {
  bookmarkId: string;
  url: string;
  title: string;
  suggestedPath: string[]; // e.g. ["Engineering", "Rust", "Crates"]
  confidence: number;      // 0.0 - 1.0
  reasoning: string;
}
```
**Constraint Prompt Rules**:
- Limit tree depth: `suggestedPath.length <= 3`.
- Do not create single-item leaf folders; group into existing categories when possible.
- Require JSON array response matching schema.

